  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="7c367623-db20-49e4-97b4-af3a44cd2e06" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Enter Questions Below this line-->
  <!--Q1-->
  <exercise data-content-id="d9e6701c-63d6-41fa-bc53-e04b99537fae" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(0.25q + 0.1d &gt; 143.88\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(0.25d + 0.1q ≥ 143.88\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0.25q + 0.1d &lt; 143.88\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0.25d + 0.1q &gt; 143.88\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(0.25q + 0.1d &gt; 143.88\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <blockquote>
        <para>This year, students in the 9th grade are collecting dimes and quarters for a school fundraiser. They are trying to collect more money than the students who were in the 9th grade last year. The students in 9th grade last year collected $143.88.</para>
      </blockquote>
      <para>Using \(d\) to represent the number of dimes collected and \(q\) to represent the number of quarters, which statement best represents this situation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The value of the quarters, \(0.25q\), plus the value of the dimes, \(0.1d\), is more than $143.88.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="09b59ea2-8e47-4950-b93c-3d3c27fe25be" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(4x − 2y &lt; 12\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(4x − 2y &gt; 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(4x − 2y &lt; 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(4x + 2y &gt; 12\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(4x + 2y &lt; 12\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which inequality is represented by the graph?</para>
      <para dir="ltr"><figure><media alt="Inequality graphed on a coordinate plane, origin O. Each axis from negative 8 to 8, by 2’s. Dashed line goes through negative 2 comma negative 10, 0 comma negative 6, and 4 comma 2. The region below the dashed line is shaded."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a1cf2edc2ae294385d8b68efdd4025a752151ae3"/></media></figure></para>
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The graph shows a dashed boundary line for the related equation \(y = 2x - 6\) and the shading is above the line. </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="56fa3e61-916e-436f-bd1e-361b975b8baa" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(200s + 500w ≤ 100,000\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(500s + 200w &lt; 100,000\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(500s + 200w ≤ 100,000\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(200s + 500w ≤ 100,000\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(200s + 500w &gt; 100,000\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For 3 - 4, use the passage below to answer the questions:</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para> A farmer is creating a budget for planting soybeans and wheat. Planting soybeans costs $200 per acre and planting wheat costs $500 per acre. He wants to spend no more than $100,000 planting soybeans and wheat.</para>
      </blockquote>
      <para>Let \(s\) represent the number of acres of soybeans and \(w\) represent the number of acres of wheat.
          Write an inequality to describe the situation.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The soybeans cost 200s dollars and the wheat costs \(500w\). The sum must be less than or equal to $100,000.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="af1ef011-ce52-496e-a059-5924974c7d45" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="(250, 100)" data-solution-options="[&quot;(200, 130)&quot;, &quot;(250, 100)&quot;, &quot;(170, 140)&quot;, &quot;(300, 90)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para> Name one solution to
          the inequality and explain what it represents in that situation.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(200(250) + 500(100) = 100,000\), which is the maximum of the farmer’s budget.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="48553143-b120-4bb4-bfc3-e5c7c5aa7f53" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(16.95d + 6.49h &lt; 50\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(16.95d + 6.49h ≥ 50\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(16.95d – 6.49h &lt; 50\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(16.95d + 6.49h &lt; 50\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(16.95d + 6.49h &gt; 50\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For 5 - 7, use the passage below to answer the questions:</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para> Amira is ordering dried chili peppers and corn husks for her cooking class. Chili peppers cost $16.95 per pound and corn husks cost $6.49 per pound.</para>
        <para> Amira spends less than $50 on \(d\) pounds of dried chili peppers and \(h\) pounds of corn husks.</para>
        <para>Here is a graph that represents this situation. </para>
        <figure><media alt="Inequality on grid."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/a759f4aa3fb063072bdd2757468a7e1efcb84fb0"/></media></figure></blockquote>
      <para>Write an
          inequality that represents this situation.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The cost of dried chili peppers, \(16.95d\), plus the cost of corn husks, 6.49h, must be less than $50.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
