<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="d4bd5ac5-0213-4f07-817f-dd15b012a935" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="87928af0-7213-40e9-8c7f-ec5beaaeb638" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Can Amira purchase 2 pounds of dried chili peppers and 4 pounds of corn husks
          and spend less than $50? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No. She would be spending \(16.95(2) + 6.49(4)\), or $59.86.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
