<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="257ec9ae-2182-43df-b153-c4a301b1b0c8" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <exercise data-content-id="8fa1b4ce-573c-418c-8d99-7cf6deb543a9" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="Yes" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Can Amira purchase 1.5 pounds of dried chili peppers and 3 pounds of corn
          husks and spend less than $50? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! Yes. She would be spending \(16.95(1.5) + 6.49(3)\), or $44.90.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
