<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="3c3e266d-902b-40b8-9a33-498f1656c45f" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a9937132-55c8-4ecf-ac34-62aa3212d11e" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(15s + 10u ≥ 200\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(15s – 10u ≥ 200\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(15s + 10u ≤ 200\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(15s + 10u ≥ 200\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(15s + 10u &lt; 200\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>For 8 - 10, use the passage below to answer the questions:</para>
      <blockquote>
        <para>A beach store rents surfboards for $15 per hour and beach umbrellas for $10 per hour. The store wants to make at least $200 per day on renting beach equipment. Let \(s\) be the number of hours that a surfboard is rented and \(u\) be the number of hours an umbrella is rented.</para>
      </blockquote>
      <para>Which inequality represents this situation?</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! The store makes \(15s\) dollars per hour renting surfboards and \(10u\) dollars renting umbrellas. The sum must be greater than or equal to $200.
      </para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Do not edit below line.-->
