</div>
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="0424bd01-10f4-4e1d-a04f-fe6b2c089de7" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q9-->
  <exercise data-content-id="be434d8c-84fb-4e60-aeb5-f281d2c0b5fc" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Can the
          beach store rent surfboards for 7 total hours and rent umbrellas for 9
          total hours and reach their goal of making $200? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No.They would be making \(15(7) + 10(9)\), or $195.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
  <!--Q10-->
  <exercise data-content-id="22ae87a4-6ce0-4a0f-92df-0a05c8da3e41" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="No" data-solution-options="[&quot;Yes&quot;, &quot;No&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Can the
          beach store rent surfboards for 10 total hours and rent umbrellas for 4
          total hours and reach their goal of making $200? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! No.They would be making \(15(10) + 10(4)\), or \($190\).</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 2.13.2 and 2.13.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  
